bin/fbink
---------
FBInk by NiLuJe — https://github.com/NiLuJe/FBInk
Licensed GPL-3.0-or-later.

This is the "kindlepw2" build (soft-float, ELF interpreter /lib/ld-linux.so.3),
extracted from KOReader release v2026.07.1:
  https://github.com/koreader/koreader/releases/tag/v2026.07.1
  koreader-kindlepw2-v2026.07.1.zip  ->  koreader/fbink

That ABI is the correct one for Paperwhite 3 firmware 5.16.2.1.1, which is the
last soft-float Kindle firmware. Do NOT replace it with a "kindlehf" / armhf
build: it will fail to start and the clock will silently fall back to eips.

As this binary is distributed under the GPL, its complete corresponding source
is available from the FBInk repository above.

